# PACKET-002 — R06-TWO-CONSUMERS: two independently installed ERP module consumers
# a/ = main-tree current state, b/ = isolated copy (Archxy 2 patch), rebuilt
# 2026-10-18 from live state. Archxy 2-owned paths ship wholesale and are not
# diffed BEFORE integration:
#  examples/rust-consumers/erp/**            (the two consumers: hospitality +
#            professional-services — TS batteries over BOTH accepted R06
#            modules (@archava/purchasing + @archava/foodservice and their
#            -pg ledgers), each with its own client.json/browser story and
#            per-consumer verify battery)
#  tools/rust/erp/module-consumers.ts        (the driver: packs the compiled
#            library, installs tarballs into scratch copies of both
#            consumers, typecheck/build/verifies, hashes the installed ERP
#            modules, refuses workspace-resolution, writes the proof JSON)
#  tools/rust/erp/module-consumers.witnesses.mjs (the witness map for the
#            manifest drift test; importable without launching tsx/npm)
#  docs/rust/archxy2/**                      (Archxy 2 doc trio + handoff)
#
# The two-consumers shape mirrors examples/crm-consumers and its driver
# (tools/crm-reference/src/consumers.ts); the proof lands in
# dist/rust-erp-module-consumers-proof.json and is bound to proof
# P-MODULE-CONSUMERS in the frozen manifest.
#
# NOTE on the packaging seam, decided by evidence: consumers install from the
# COMPILED npm library tarballs (tools/library/pack.mjs already ships
# @archava/purchasing-pg + @archava/foodservice-pg — 62 packages pack green in
# this copy). The cargo-tarball route (cargo package -p archava-domain) was
# probed first and does NOT work offline — the packaged verify build searches
# crates.io for the unpublished path-only archava-core even with a version on
# the workspace dependency and a [patch.crates-io] present — so NO
# rust/Cargo.toml change rides in this packet; the workspace stays
# byte-identical to main.
#
# VERIFIED IN THE COPY (2026-10-18): `pnpm erp:verify-consumers` PASS end to
# end (pack 62 packages → both consumers typecheck/build/verify green from
# node_modules, implementations hash-identical, workspace resolution
# refused), node --test tools/rust/test/verify-release.test.mjs 23/23,
# node --test tools/rust/test/verify.test.mjs 20/20.
#
# INTEGRATION BASIS: main has not integrated PACKET-000/001 yet (re-verified
# 2026-10-17), and they touch NONE of the five files here except
# docs/rust/required-coverage.json — which PACKET-002 edits at a DIFFERENT
# proof (P-MODULE-CONSUMERS vs P-ERP-*) — so all three packets fold
# independently in any order.

